# Copy to benchmark/.env and edit. .env is gitignored so tokens stay local:
#
#   cp benchmark/.env.example benchmark/.env
#
# This layer sits above the profile and defaults.env, and below the real
# environment, so `PROFILE=granite ./benchmark.sh` and
# `./benchmark.sh PROFILE=granite` both still win over whatever is written here.
# See defaults.env for the settings that do not change with the model, and
# profiles/ for the ones that do.
#
# Plain KEY=VALUE only -- no quoting, no shell expansion, no inline comments.

# Match whatever the server was started with: the profile supplies the model
# name, and vLLM rejects a request naming a model it is not serving.
# ../benchmark_sweep.sh exports PROFILE so both halves agree on their own.
# PROFILE=granite

# Set this only to name a checkpoint no profile names -- it outranks the profile.
# MODEL_ID=deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813

# Where the server is. Defaults to localhost:8000; set BASE_URL instead when the
# endpoint needs a scheme or path the host/port pair cannot express.
# HOST=localhost
# PORT=8000
# BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1

# vLLM ignores the key, but a gateway in front of it may not.
# API_KEY=EMPTY
